      ⍴Z
0

      ⍝ Bugs28 #57 regression (Bugs27 #56 residual): dyadic ¨ (like
      ⍝ ∘.f, f⍤y, and f.g) still broke when the operand changed ⎕IO --
      ⍝ Z__vA_LO_EACH_vB/sB and Z__sA_LO_EACH_vB (Macro.def) indexed
      ⍝ μ1/μ2/μ6 with the raw loop counter μ8, seeded from ⎕IO ONCE at
      ⍝ the start; if LO's own ⎕IO←0 (global, not auto-localized in a
      ⍝ lambda) persisted past its first call, every later iteration's
      ⍝ indexing (relative to the NEW ⎕IO) silently misaligned instead
      ⍝ of INDEX-ERROR-ing outright, unlike the ALREADY-fixed monadic ¨
      ⍝ (Z__LO_EACH_B). Fixed the same self-correcting way: recompute
      ⍝ ⎕IO+(μ8-savedIO) fresh at each use instead of trusting μ8 alone.
      ⍝ 1+⍳2 (⎕IO=0) = 1 2; 2+⍳3 (⎕IO now 0 from the first call, but
      ⍝ self-correctingly still right) = 2 3 4.
      ⍝
      ]FILE_CTL SKIP_APL2   ⍝ lambdas are a GNU APL extension
      1 2 {⎕IO←0 ⋄ ⍺+⍳⍵}¨ 2 3
 1 2  2 3 4 

      ]FILE_CTL NO_SKIP
      ⎕IO←1

      ⍝ Bugs30 #1 regression: L LO¨ R as a selective-assignment target.
      ⍝
      ⍝ A NULL lvalue (an over-take of an empty vector, 1↑V for empty
      ⍝ V) used to segfault Bif_OPER1_EACH::eval_ALB instead of
      ⍝ erroring cleanly; fixed by guarding dest==0 the same way the
      ⍝ already-fixed monadic branch does (see Each_monadic.tc). No
      ⍝ display after these: a selective assignment produces none
      ⍝ (LRM p.41).

      V←⍬
      (1⌽¨1↑V)←1
INDEX ERROR
      (1⌽¨1↑V)←1
       ^^

      ⍝ leaves an )SI entry for the failed immediate execution above.
      ⍝
      )SIC

      ⍝ a genuinely selecting primitive LO (Function::get_selectivity(),
      ⍝ SEL_DYADIC bit) must still work end to end: ⌽ (rotate) does.

      V←,5
      (1⌽¨1↑V)←1
      V
1

      ⍝ a primitive LO that does NOT select -- + (scalar) computes a new
      ⍝ value from B's content instead of selecting a position in it, so
      ⍝ it can never work as a selective-assignment target regardless of
      ⍝ the target's validity. Before get_selectivity() this reached
      ⍝ ScalarFunction's own evaluation and DOMAIN-ERRORed on a raw
      ⍝ LvalCell it could not interpret -- an accident of implementation,
      ⍝ not a principled rejection (see Bugs30 #1 write-up); now rejected
      ⍝ up front with the same SYNTAX ERROR a defined LO gets below.

      V2←,5
      (1 2+¨1↑V2)←1 2
SYNTAX ERROR
      (1 2+¨1↑V2)←1 2
       ^          ^
      V2
5

      ⍝ leaves an )SI entry for the failed immediate execution above.
      ⍝
      )SIC

      ⍝ a defined LO must never see a selective-assignment target's
      ⍝ live LvalCell (it could smuggle it out into unrelated storage
      ⍝ via an ordinary side effect and leave a dangling reference
      ⍝ once the original array is freed); reject it up front instead,
      ⍝ for both operands of a dyadic each.

      KLAM←{⍺}
      W←1 2 3
      (1 1 1 KLAM¨W)←9 9 9
SYNTAX ERROR
      (1 1 1 KLAM¨W)←9 9 9
       ^             ^

      ⍝ leaves an )SI entry for the failed immediate execution above.
      ⍝
      )SIC
      )ERASE KLAM

